From d5d199e3614e28a4b1c67598a4e3fbc7b4beb866 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: soulexit <metehan.tanriverdi01@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:04:03 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 81/84] panvk/jm: adjacency without a GS, null index buffers,
 polygon-mode depth bias

Three dEQP-VK groups that failed on the Mali-G76 (JM v7), plus a draw
helper bug the regress run found:

- *_with_adjacency topologies without a geometry shader: translate_prim()
  has no adjacency modes on v7 (the tiler has none), so these draws hit
  UNREACHABLE and the tiler got a garbage draw mode (wrong pixels or
  DEVICE_LOST). They now go through the passthrough GS of their adjacency
  class, which drops the adjacent vertices; passthrough_gs() builds it for
  a screen-space vertex shader too.
- maintenance6 + nullDescriptor null index buffer: v7 bound address 0
  (faulted) with size 0 (indirect draws were skipped). It now binds the
  device's zero page with its size (PANVK_NULL_ZERO_SIZE, moved to
  panvk_device.h).
- Depth bias in LINE/POINT polygon mode: the polygon-mode passthrough emits
  lines/points, which the tiler does not bias. The GS now computes the bias
  of each triangle the way llvmpipe does and adds it to clip z. The
  parameters use the panvk_gs_push padding words.
- draw_helper.cl: an indexed indirect draw that reads no index (indexCount 0
  or only restart indices) wrapped vertex_range to 2 or ~2^32 and ran the
  vertex job at a vertex index near 2^32. Such a draw now gets NULL jobs.

P40: the 121 adjacency, 16 maintenance6 and 1616 depth_bias cases all pass
or are NotSupported. regress.txt: 18847 pass, 1 fail
(memory_model.message_passing.permuted_index.barrier, also in the
1004poff baseline).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
